<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malerkotla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malerkotla is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, the seat of the former princely state of the same name ruled by Afghan nawabs. It is the only Muslim-majority town in Indian Punjab, a status linked to the tradition that its nawab Sher Muhammad Khan protested in 1705 against the execution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guru-gobind-singh">Guru Gobind Singh</a>'s young sons. In 2021 it became the headquarters of a new district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malerkotla.jpg" alt="Malerkotla" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khalid G A · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kuka_Martyrs_Memorial,_Malerkotla_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
